[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

Cut-by-cut butchering for [b]Build 42[/b]. Hang the carcass, pick a primal from a diagram of the animal, and trace the cut yourself while the knife drifts. Every cut comes out with a hidden grade and a realistic weight, from a whole cow down to a rabbit. Then cure it, dry it, and render the fat into tallow, lard, candles and soap.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes, dedicated servers included. The server decides every cut[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes. Only carcasses you butcher after enabling it are affected[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Works with[/b][/td][td]Dazed Cooking, Dazed Climate, Dazed Plumbing (all optional)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedButchery[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-cut.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/cut.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Cows, pigs, sheep and deer go on a butcher hook. Bleed them with vanilla's Bleed button first (an unbled carcass caps every grade at 75), then press [b]Open Butchery[/b].
[*]Chickens, turkeys and rabbits use vanilla's [b]Butcher[/b] option, which now opens the Butchery window.
[*]Skin or pluck first: until the hide is off, the whole body is one target.
[*]Pick a primal and press [b]Cut[/b]. Drag from the green marker to the red one; the knife wanders, and rushing makes it wander more.
[*]Hold on past the red marker and you cut into the next primal, lowering its grade and yield.
[*]Knife cuts need a knife, saw cuts a saw, cleaver cuts a cleaver or hatchet. A worn or dull tool drifts more.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-grades.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/grades.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Every cut gets a hidden grade from 0 to 100: your trace, the tool, bleeding, hanging time, freshness and the animal's condition.
[*]The grade sets weight, food values and spoil time. At Butchering 2 you see the tier (Prime, Choice, Select, Standard, Poor), at 6 the number.
[*]Yields follow live weight, size and the meat-ratio gene. A full-size cow gives about 220 kg of cuts.
[*]Offal, meat scraps, fat and cleaned intestines from large animals. Heads, blood and bones stay vanilla.
[*]A [b]Butcher's Log[/b] keeps your cuts, Prime cuts, overcuts and best grade per animal.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-field.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/field.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Field Dress[/b] a large animal on the ground with a knife for its offal and twice the freshness, then [b]Quarter[/b] it with a saw.
[*]Right-click a quarter at home to [b]Open Butchery[/b] on its half of each primal.
[*]Quarters carried by hand, in a bag or loose in a vehicle bruise and lose grade. Drag them on a [b]Butcher's Hand Sled[/b], or hang them on a [b]Game Cart[/b], a small rack trailer any vehicle can tow.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-aging.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/aging.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Each cut dulls your knife, cleaver or saw a little. Right-click it to [b]Hone Butcher's Edge[/b] on a whetstone. Vanilla sharpness is untouched.
[*][b]Dry-age[/b] a Choice or Prime cut in a fridge for a day or more, then trim it for a better grade.
[*][b]Cold keeps meat:[/b] carcasses and quarters spoil by the temperature around them. Frozen they barely age, near 0 °C they age at a third of the speed, and a hot day spoils them fast. A deer hung outside in winter keeps for days.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-preserve.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/preserve.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Mince, cured bacon, cured ham, sausages, jerky, bone meal and blood-and-bone fertilizer. Grades carry over.
[*][b]Render fat[/b]: chop fat into a cooking pot, cook it on any stove, campfire or barbecue, then [b]Strain Rendered Fat[/b]. Suet gives 3 tallow, pork fat gives 3 lard and 2 cracklings.
[*]Tallow or lard makes [b]tallow candles[/b] and [b]lye soap[/b].
[*][b]Jerky needs drying[/b] with [b]Dazed Cooking[/b]: Make Jerky gives Salted Meat Strips that dry into jerky on a drying rack, in a food dehydrator or in Dazed Plumbing's smoker. Without Cooking, jerky is ready at once.
[*]Five magazines in loot. Four primal guides steady your knife on their animals; [i]Curing and Smoking Quarterly[/i] teaches the cures.
[/list]

The in-game [b]Dazed Mod Suite Guide[/b] from Dazed Core has a Butchery tab.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-sandbox.png?v=2[/img]
52 options on the Dazed Butchery page: yield, the cutting minigame (or turn it off and grade by skill), drift, overcut distance, tool rules and wear, grade caps, carcass life, offal and scraps, grade visibility, hook rules, XP, cut time, pausing in single player, the multiplayer claim time, edge wear, sounds, blood, magazines, dry-aging, field dressing, quarters, hauling and temperature spoilage.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-compat.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only.
[*]Covers cows, pigs, sheep, deer, chickens, turkeys and rabbits. Rats, mice, raccoons and other mods' animals use vanilla butchering.
[*]In multiplayer, a carcass belongs to whoever opens it until they close the window or the claim runs out.
[*]With [b]Dazed Climate[/b], spoilage and dry-aging read its room temperatures, so a cold cellar keeps meat. [b]Dazed Cooking[/b] cooks every cut its own way and dries your jerky.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Butchery/images/h-help.png?v=2[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab. Include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

